# Generated QBER telemetry streams are large and fully reproducible from a
# fixed seed (see qkd_sim/qber_stream.py) — regenerate with:
#   python -m qkd_sim.qber_stream --out data/qber_train.csv --rounds 7000 --seed 42
data/*.csv
models/benchmark_rounds.csv

# Trained model weights, quantized TFLite artifacts, and benchmark/metric
# reports ARE committed (see models/) so the repo is inspectable without a
# full retrain — they are small (<500KB total).

# OS/editor cruft
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Q-Safe Field Link demo output. The replay page, the measured report and the
# figures ARE committed -- they are the offline fallback and the evidence pack,
# and they are small. The raw event trace is ~1 MB and fully regenerable with
# `python -m demo.record_demo`, and the self-signed TLS material is per-machine.
demo_output/demo_session.json
demo_output/tls/

